From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Give the chipset a core of its own

Every secondary core reaches the WFE at the end of secondary_boot() and
stays there for the life of the machine: PISTORM_ANY_MODEL is not defined
on this build, so three quarters of a Pi 3 is switched off.

That matters because a chipset costing 250 ns per colour clock, against
the 282 ns realtime wants, takes 88.7% of whatever core it shares. On one
core a fast CPU and a realtime chipset cannot both exist. On two they can.

Core 2, which is where upstream puts its own housekeeper on PiStorm
builds. The entry point returns if Bellatrix does not want the core, and
then this falls through to the same WFE as before.
---
 src/aarch64/start.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
diff --git a/src/aarch64/start.c b/src/aarch64/start.c
--- a/src/aarch64/start.c
+++ b/src/aarch64/start.c
@@ -488,6 +488,43 @@
     (void)async_log;
 #endif
 
+#if defined(BELLATRIX_EMU68) && CONFIG_RIGEL
+    /*
+     * The chipset gets a core of its own.
+     *
+     * Without this every secondary core reaches the WFE below and stays there
+     * for the life of the machine: PISTORM_ANY_MODEL is not defined on this
+     * build, so three quarters of a Pi 3 is switched off. Meanwhile a chipset
+     * that costs 250 ns per colour clock, against the 282 ns realtime wants,
+     * takes 88.7% of whatever core it shares -- so on one core a fast CPU and
+     * a realtime chipset cannot both exist. On two they can, and the second
+     * one is already sitting here doing nothing.
+     *
+     * Core 2, which is where upstream puts its own housekeeper on PiStorm
+     * builds, so the placement is not a new claim about what is free.
+     *
+     * The entry point returns if Bellatrix does not want the core -- the
+     * chipset may not be enabled at run time -- and then this falls through to
+     * the same WFE as before. AI_context/issues/ISSUE-0074.md.
+     */
+    if (cpu_id == 2)
+    {
+        extern void bellatrix_chipset_core_entry(void);
+        bellatrix_chipset_core_entry();
+    }
+
+    /*
+     * And core 3 drains the console. Every core that logs pushes a finished
+     * line into a ring of its own and returns; someone has to be the one that
+     * waits on the UART, and it must not be a core with work to do.
+     */
+    if (cpu_id == 3)
+    {
+        extern void amiga_console_run_on_core(void);
+        amiga_console_run_on_core();
+    }
+#endif
+
     while(1) { __asm__ volatile("wfe"); }
 }
 uintptr_t vid_base;
